invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_mont64_blocks.c
catches: rsa_blocks_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_blocks_reduce drops the carry out of a block's second
  chain, the chain that adds the carry from the block below. That chain
  carries out only when four words of the value equal four words of the
  modulus, which no product of random words meets, so every
  multiplication still agrees with the loops. bin/rsa_blocks_equiv_test
  hands the last subtraction the modulus itself, where every block's
  second chain carries, and its words then differ from the loops'.

--- old
        carry = high + (uint64_t)(sum >> 64);
    }
    // top:a - m borrows when top is zero and a - m borrowed. The sum below carries when it did
--- new
        carry = high;
    }
    // top:a - m borrows when top is zero and a - m borrowed. The sum below carries when it did
